        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0575" n="1309" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1309"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Terrell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 632.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your Nos. 627 and 630, of
                    the 18th and 24th ultimo, respectively, in relation lo the case of Melcoun
                    Guedjian.</p>
                <p>The Department’s cablegram [of September 26] seems to cover all the essential
                    points in regard to which you ask instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
